course: dictionary
lesson: 8714
title: Sensible and its many shades
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sensible means having good judgement. A sensible person thinks before acting and makes wise, safe choices. «Whenever Alice asks a sensible question, the two creatures call her dull» tells us her question was wise, even though the creatures do not think so.
explain: Sensible can also describe things. Sensible clothes or shoes are practical and comfortable, not fancy. «Studies have found that banknotes and coins can carry more germs than a toilet seat, so washing hands after handling money is sensible» means it is a wise, safe thing to do.
explain: Watch out for French. In French, sensible means sensitive, easily upset or touched. In English it does not mean that. Check the sentence: «Adults usually know more, so listening to them is sensible» shows that sensible means wise, not upset.
fact: Sensible means having good judgement and making wise, safe choices.
fact: Sensible can also describe clothes or shoes that are practical and comfortable rather than fancy.
fact: Useful phrases: a sensible idea, be sensible, the sensible thing to do.
fact: In French, «sensible» means sensitive. In English, it means wise or practical.
fact: A sensible question is a wise question, even if other people do not appreciate it.
exercise: What does sensible mean? | *Having good judgement and making wise, safe choices | Very loud | Easily upset or touched | Fancy and expensive
exercise: «Washing hands after handling money is sensible.» Why? | Because soap is fancy | Because money is always clean | Because money is heavy | *Because coins and notes can carry germs, so it is a wise, safe choice
exercise: Clara says sensible shoes are fancy shoes with sparkles. Is she right? | No, sensible shoes are practical and comfortable | Yes, they are very expensive | *No, but they are sparkly | Yes, sensible shoes sparkle
test: In French, sensible means sensitive. What does «sensible» mean in English? | *Wise and practical | Easily upset | Very loud | Shiny
test: «Whenever Alice asks a sensible question, the two creatures call her dull.» What does sensible tell us about Alice's question? | It was lost | It was rude | *It was wise and good | It was silly
exam: «To avoid mix-ups, pilots, ships, scientists and games use one world time, UTC.» Why is using one world time sensible? | It is fancy and expensive | It is only for pilots | *It avoids mix-ups and confusion | It makes the clocks run faster
